e/organ_atlas.json::organs[routing_anti_patterns_registry].principle_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"world_model_projection_drift_control_room","ref_kind":"principle","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[world_model_projection_drift_control_room].principle_refs"}],"cited_by_count":32,"component_ids":["batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule","batch10_governance_compilers_capsule","batch10_live_source_drift_capsule","batch11_saturation_engines_capsule","batch12_market_dashboard_read_model_capsule","batch12_prediction_market_board_capsule","batch4_proof_authority_runtime","batch5_authority_systems_capsule","batch6_unsurfaced_primitives_capsule","batch7_demo_take_console_capsule","batch7_macro_engines_capsule","batch7_oracle_sibling_capsule","batch7_secondary_runtime_capsule","batch8_audio_level_rms_port","batch8_compliance_pipeline_capsule","batch8_policy_engines_capsule","batch8_structural_theses_capsule","batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","batch8_validator_checker_capsule","batch9_macro_engines_capsule","bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","cognitive_operator_registry","cold_reader_route_map","durable_agent_work_landing_replay","engine_room_demo","macro_projection_import_protocol","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","public_reveal_walkthrough","routing_anti_patterns_registry","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":[],"id":"P-5","kind":"principle","plain":"A saved result, command output, source import or work-landing attempt that may be reused must record a hash of the exact content it was computed from. Any change to the source bytes, to uncommitted files in its scope, to the parent commit or to the fixture input means it has to be recomputed.","principles":[],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The serial number covers only matching the exact item; it leaves out other kinds of change the rule watches for, such as edited files or a moved parent commit.","maps":[{"analogy":"the warranty holds only while the serial number matches the unit","doctrine":"reuse only when the saved content tag matches the current inputs"},{"analogy":"trusting the model name on the box instead of the serial number","doctrine":"a matching name or label allowing reuse"}],"text":"A warranty covers the exact unit whose serial number is on the claim. If a part with a different serial number was swapped in, the matching model name on the box does not carry the warranty over."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A resumed landing attempt reuses an earlier result because the task name matches, although the parent commit and the files in scope have changed.","does_not_prove":"These reuse paths record their inputs, and one known case where the recorded input and the current input can disagree is still open.","enforced_in_component_ids":["macro_projection_import_protocol","durable_agent_work_landing_replay"],"example":{"component_ids":["macro_projection_import_protocol"],"text":"The source-import protocol brings public material in with a manifest and a hash for each file, so when the source bytes change the imported copy is recomputed instead of being reused under the same name."},"governs":"The point where an earlier result is about to be reused instead of recomputed.","plain":"A saved result can be reused only if it is tagged with the exact inputs it was made from and those inputs still match. If the inputs have changed, the work has to be redone, whatever the name or label says.","potential_misread":"That a matching name or path means the cached answer is still good, when only a match on the content it was computed from allows reuse.","refuses":"Serving a cached result looked up by name, path or label after the content behind it has changed.","requires":"A hash of the input content saved with the result, reuse only when that hash still matches, and a recompute or refusal as soon as the source, files in scope, parent commit or fixture input change.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"A stale or tampered result cannot be served as fresh just because its name or path still looks familiar."},"rests_on":["AX-4"],"source_ref":"PRINCIPLES.md::P-5","statement":"Grounding: AX-4.\nObligation grounding: AX-4.O1.content_basis_digest_declared, AX-4.O2.equal_basis_permits_reuse, AX-4.O3.digest_drift_forces_recompute, AX-4.O4.freshness_basis_mismatch_materialized.\n\nA saved result, command output, source import or work-landing attempt that may\nbe reused must record a hash of the exact content it was computed from. Any\nchange to the source bytes, to uncommitted files in its scope, to the parent\ncommit or to the fixture input means it has to be recomputed.","statement_sha256":"df22c911f55379306588e9a6f4436c4eb709edefad9bc1c63c44dc57558ada0f","title":"Cache by content, not by name","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}